  "instructions": [
    "Heat olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat.",
    "Add the onion, carrot, and celery and sauté until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Stir in the garlic, fennel seeds, and lemon zest and cook for 1 minute.",
    "Add the turkey necks and brown on all sides, 3 to 4 minutes per side.",
    "Pour in the white wine and let it reduce by half, about 3 minutes.",
    "Stir in the tomato paste and coconut milk, then add the chicken broth.",
    "Season with salt and pepper, bring the mixture to a gentle simmer, cover, and cook for 30 minutes until the turkey necks are tender.",
    "Remove the lid, stir in fresh thyme, and let the sauce thicken for 5 minutes.",
    "Plate the casserole and garnish with chopped parsley.",
    "Serve hot.",
    "Ensure poultry is cooked to an internal temperature of 74°C / 165°F (juices run clear, no pink remaining) before serving."
